1148+ B5FB              ; ================================================================
1149+ B5FB              ; svc_read_at: read a byte range of the file being viewed into RAM.
1150+ B5FB              ;   C  = destination 8K page (a number out of VIEWCTX_DATA_PAGES),
1151+ B5FB              ;   HL = offset inside that page (0-8191), DE = byte count,
1152+ B5FB              ;   source offset bits 0-15 in VIEWCTX_EXTRACT_OFF, bits 16-31 in
1153+ B5FB              ;   VIEWCTX_EXTRACT_OFHI.
1154+ B5FB              ; Returns A = 0 and carry clear on success; 4 = open, 5 = seek, 6 = read.
1155+ B5FB              ;
1156+ B5FB              ; The viewer preloads only the first 64KB of a file, which is no use to a
1157+ B5FB              ; plugin whose index sits at the end - a ZIP keeps its directory there.
1158+ B5FB              ; DOS_READ pages by 16K bank, so the 8K page has to be split into the
1159+ B5FB              ; bank number and the address that half of it appears at.
